# EmptySock Engine — Cursor / Windsurf Rules

You are working on a game built with EmptySock (@emptysock/engine).
TypeScript strict mode. 2D primary (PixiJS v8 + Rapier2D + Howler.js). Optional 3D via Three.js. Tauri v2 shell.

## Absolute rules

NEVER import pixi.js, @dimforge/rapier2d, howler, or three directly.
NEVER use `any` type. Use `unknown` + Zod or type guards.
NEVER use `!` non-null assertions. Use `?.` and `?? fallback`.
NEVER use setTimeout or setInterval in game logic. Use Timer.after() or Timer.every().
NEVER use async/await inside onUpdate() or onFixedUpdate(). Use function* coroutines.
NEVER access the DOM directly. Use the engine UI system.
ALWAYS call entity.destroy() when entities are no longer needed.
ALWAYS cancel TimerHandles in onDestroy() if they reference scene objects.
ALWAYS parse external/saved JSON through a Zod schema before use.
ALWAYS add explicit return types to functions.
ALWAYS commit with conventional format: feat/fix/refactor/chore(scope): message

## Core API — quick reference

Engine.create({ scenes, startScene, gameSpeed }) then engine.start()

Scene base class:
  onLoad(): Promise<void>     — async setup, awaited before render
  onUpdate(dt: number): void  — every frame, dt = seconds
  onDestroy(): void           — cleanup before unload

entity = scene.createEntity('name')
entity.addComponent(Type, props)
entity.getComponent(Type)          → T | undefined
entity.requireComponent(Type)      → T | throws
entity.hasTag(tag)                 → boolean
entity.destroy()

Input.isDown(key)          — held
Input.isPressed(key)       — just pressed this frame
Input.isReleased(key)      — just released this frame
Input.axis('Horizontal')   — -1 to 1
Input.pointer.position     — { x, y }

Audio.play(id, opts?)
Audio.music(id, opts?)
Audio.setGroupVolume(group, vol)

Camera.follow(entity, opts?)
Camera.shake(opts)
Camera.zoom(scale, opts?)
Camera.fade(opts) / Camera.unfade(opts?)

SceneManager.load(name)
SceneManager.transition(name, { effect, duration })
SceneManager.push(name) / SceneManager.pop()

Timer.after(seconds, fn)   → TimerHandle
Timer.every(seconds, fn)   → TimerHandle
handle.cancel()

entity.startCoroutine(function* () {
  yield waitSeconds(1.0)
  yield waitUntil(() => condition)
  yield waitForEvent('eventName')
})

SaveSystem.save(slot, data)
SaveSystem.load(slot)       → { data: unknown } — always Zod parse before use

t(key, vars?)               — localisation lookup
LocalisationSystem.setLocale(code)

TilemapSystem.load(file)    → map
map.getLayer(name).enablePhysics()

Tween.to(target, props, { duration, ease })
Profiler.getStats()         → { fps, drawCalls, frameTime, memoryMB }
Engine.gpuTier              → 'potato' | 'low' | 'mid' | 'high' | 'ultra'

## Performance — Pi 4 and mobile targets

Keep draw calls under 50/frame on 'low' tier.
Use texture atlases to batch sprites sharing the same texture.
Use ObjectPool for high-frequency entities (bullets, particles).
Avoid object allocation inside onUpdate() — reuse private fields.
Disable soft shadows on 'potato' and 'low' GPU tiers.

## Full reference

skills/          — per-system skill files
docs/            — human-readable guides
ai/api-reference.json — full typed API
